## Context

`slides/manuscript/main.md:213` (Annex C header note) says:

> *the conjectured-results paragraph in §4 will be replaced by an
> observed-results paragraph when 0199 completes*

PR #405 inserted a *First observation (Mistral pilot, n=1 agent)*
paragraph alongside the existing *Conjectured results* paragraph in
§4 (lines 59–63). The Annex C caveat now technically mis-states the
structure: §4 carries TWO paragraphs (conjecture + pilot
observation), and 0199 should subsume both.

The §4 first-observation paragraph self-labels as "Mistral pilot,
n=1 agent" — the framing is honest. The inconsistency is only in
how Annex C describes the future replacement.

## Actions

1. Rewrite line 213 to acknowledge the two-paragraph structure, e.g.:
   *"The conjectured-results and first-observation paragraphs in §4
   will be subsumed by an observed-results paragraph when 0199
   completes."*

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Annex C header note updated.
- [ ] No other Annex C / §4 prose contradicts the structure.
